  "source_scope_note": "The selected problem is exact original first main Theorem4.30: the stable-limit nonsymmetric Macdonald functions indexed by reduced compositions and partitions form a simultaneous Cherednik weight basis of almost-symmetric functions over Q(q,t). Complete author Sections1--4 retain the precise almost-symmetric spaces, Ion--Wu convergence/operator definitions, full appended-zero convergence, stable eigenvalues, lowering construction, nonzero stable symmetrized images and complete independence proof1082--1092. Named standard DAHA/HHL/Macdonald identities remain original references. Later recurrence and extra power-sum operator constructions are unselected in this ID and kept only as their exact printed references. The single fixed numerical augmented filling is an exact original diagram-only crop, with all absent-cell positions retained; every surrounding general HHL/statistic formula, definition and human proof remains editable. Exactly four literal mathbbm{1} indicator symbols at194/358/639/640 use root-approved pinned Noto U+1D7D9 mathord with proportional text/script math styles; exponents/function arguments unchanged, other arguments reject, visible stroke/width/placement differences disclosed. No denied package acquisition or generalized tableau/bbm emulation is supplied.",
